# Only a value that copies is copied out of a view (Core §4), or by
# `[n of x]`, `fill`, `|+x|`, or `??` and `?` through a view: a struct
# that holds a Cell is unique, one that holds a write view has one
# holder, and one that owns a resource moves. A copy out of a read view
# never hands on a write view the value holds, which would write
# through the read view.

